# /plan-design-review — designer's-eye review

Walk a design doc through 7 passes, rate each 0–10, fix gaps via inline plan edits, re-rate. Target 10. Issue **one AskUserQuestion per finding** — never batch. Reads `DESIGN.md` as source of truth.

## Pre-audit

```bash
# Most recent design doc on this branch (from /office-hours)
DESIGN_DOC=$(ls -t "${SMRITI_HOME:-$HOME/.smriti}/projects/$SLUG/"*-"$BRANCH_SLUG"-design-*.md 2>/dev/null | head -1)
[ -z "$DESIGN_DOC" ] && { echo "/plan-design-review: no design doc found for branch '$BRANCH'. Run /office-hours first."; exit 0; }

# DESIGN.md is source of truth; warn if missing
if [ ! -f DESIGN.md ]; then
  echo "WARN: DESIGN.md is missing. Recommend /design-consultation first to lock in the system, then re-run."
fi

# UI scope detection — does the design doc actually involve UI?
grep -iE 'ui|screen|page|component|view|button|form|layout|responsive|mobile|desktop' "$DESIGN_DOC" >/dev/null \
  || { echo "/plan-design-review: this design doc has no UI scope (no ui/screen/page/component mentions). Skipping."; exit 0; }
```

If the user passes `--force`, run anyway.

